        "article_text_excerpt": "The decision to shoot down the drone was made to prevent it from posing a threat to people in Latvia, Defence Minister Raivis Melnis told LETA. “The decision to shoot down the drone was made taking into account the danger it posed. Drones entering Latvian territory can endanger our residents, therefore they must be destroyed,” the minister stressed, adding that there was no way to guarantee that an unmanned aerial vehicle would simply crash somewhere in a swamp or forest. He also dismissed concerns voiced by some residents that several drones, rather than just one, had allegedly been spotted. Melnis explained that only one drone had been detected, while residents may have mistaken the noise generated by accelerating fighter jets for additional aircraft. early on Friday morning allied fighter jets shot down an unmanned aerial vehicle that had entered Latvian airspace near Lake Boževa, approximately five kilometres from the centre of Rugāji in Balvi Municipality, Sandra Kapteine, head of",
